<BaseLayout title="About" description="Tampa Curated is an independent editorial concept about the people, places, and ideas defining a more interesting city."><PageIntro number="06" title="AN INDEPENDENT EYE" deck="For the places with a point of view. The people making something happen. The city beyond the obvious."/><div class="about-layout"><div class="about-art"><span class="eyebrow">OUR POINT OF VIEW / 001</span><h2>LOCAL<br/>BY CHOICE.<br/>CURIOUS<br/>BY NATURE.</h2><span aria-hidden="true">✳</span></div><div class="prose"><h2>Look a little closer.</h2><p>Tampa Curated is an independent cultural publication in the making. We’re interested in the city’s restaurants and studios, its late-night rooms and early-morning rituals, and the people giving those places their character.</p><p>We believe a good recommendation begins with attention. A visit. A conversation. A detail worth remembering. Our ambition is to make a publication that feels considered, personal, and unmistakably of this place.</p><h2>The first edition is a beginning.</h2><p>This website is a fully working demonstration of that publication. Its profiles are fictional, its business listings are invented examples, and its editorial essays illustrate a direction rather than verified reporting. Stock portraits do not depict the fictional people named alongside them.</p><p>The neighborhood names are real. The guides are sample introductions, and some photographs illustrate a mood rather than a specific location. Image captions make those distinctions explicit.</p><h2>How we’ll work.</h2><p>Real coverage will be grounded in firsthand visits and approved interviews. We will verify practical details, credit photographers, distinguish editorial decisions from paid work, and correct errors openly.</p><p>No business has paid to appear in this demonstration, and no ranking, endorsement, or operating detail should be inferred from it.</p><h2>Keep in touch.</h2><p>Our newsletter, public contact address, and social channels are coming soon. We’ll add working contact details when the publication is ready.</p><a class="text-link" href={url('credits/')}>Photography & type credits <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><Newsletter/></BaseLayout>
